        <tr>
          <td class="py-2">11ty</td>
          <td>Excellent</td>
          <td>Good</td>
          <td>Good</td>
        </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p>
      Vercel obviously wins for Next.js. Netlify has the best general support across different frameworks. Cloudflare is
      catching up but some framework adapters are still community-maintained.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- How to Choose -->
  <section id="how-to-choose">
    <h2>How to Choose</h2>
    <p>
      Let me make this simple. Pick based on your primary use case:
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-4 my-6">
      <div class="bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
        <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">Choose Netlify if...</h4>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mt-2">You want the most polished experience that works with everything. Great
          for agencies, freelancers, and anyone who deploys lots of different projects. Form handling and identity are
          nice bonuses.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
        <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">Choose Vercel if...</h4>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mt-2">You are building with Next.js or want the absolute smoothest React deploy
          experience. The integration is unbeatable. Just be aware of the commercial use restrictions on free tier.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
        <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">Choose Cloudflare Pages if...</h4>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mt-2">Bandwidth costs matter or you need edge compute with Workers. The free tier
          is unbeatable. Also great if you already use Cloudflare for DNS or CDN.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
        <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">Choose GitHub Pages if...</h4>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mt-2">Your project is open source and you just want it online with zero extra
          accounts. Documentation sites especially. Cannot beat the simplicity.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

