  <!-- Conclusion -->
  <section id="conclusion">
    <h2>Conclusion</h2>
    <p>
      Five years, 50+ projects, three platforms. <strong>Netlify</strong> is still my default. Solid across the board, works
      with everything, never really lets me down. The form handling alone saves me from setting up backends.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Vercel</strong> when it is a Next.js project. The integration is just too smooth to ignore. ISR, image
      optimization, edge middleware. It all just works.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong> when I need that unlimited bandwidth or Workers for edge logic. The free tier is
      genuinely the best value if you can deal with the slightly rougher experience.
    </p>
    <p>
      Honestly though, you cannot really go wrong with any of them. They are all light-years ahead of traditional hosting.
      Pick one, start deploying, and switch later if you need to. It is not a permanent decision.
    </p>

    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-ocean-deep/40 to-jet-stream/20 border border-jet-stream/30 rounded-xl p-6 mt-6">
      <p class="text-white font-semibold">My Top Pick: Netlify</p>
      <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mt-2">Best overall static hosting experience for developers. Works with any
        framework, excellent documentation, and a generous free tier.</p>
      <div class="mt-4">
        <AffiliateButton
            href="/go/netlify"
            text="Start Deploying Free"
            subtext="100GB bandwidth included"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

